Table~\ref{tab:reviewer-selected} and
Figure~\ref{fig:halfspace-two-parameter-results} show that DD reduces
persistent storage by \(@@SAVING@@\%\), from \(@@GLOBAL_PAYLOAD@@\)
to \(@@DD_PAYLOAD@@\) MiB, while maintaining comparable mean
online time: \(@@DD_TIME@@\) s versus \(@@GLOBAL_TIME@@\) s for global.
All nine queries reach \(10^{-10}\) after the SL steps. DD is
\(@@SPEEDUP@@\) times faster than shifted ILU, although sparse direct
solution remains faster at this two-dimensional size.
